                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "pvc":</h3><p><b>PVC</b> or <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyvinyl_chloride">polyvinyl chloride</a> is a form of plastic commonly used in numerous household and construction applications, e.g. plumbing pipe. </p><p>PVC was used by <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Neumann">Neumann</a> and <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Microtech-Gefell">Gefell</a> in the manufacture of many early condenser microphone capsules, perhaps most famously the <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/tag/m7">M7</a>. Gefell continues to manufacture the M7 with PVC diaphragms today.</p><p>Most modern condenser microphone diaphragms are made of thin polyester film (usually 1-6 microns thick) such as Mylar.</p>
